We reduced inventory from +14 to -2 with skew 0.8 at minimal P&L cost, but buys are adversely selected (69% adverse, -2.3 markout) vs sells very profitable, suggesting downside informed flow amid rising volatility. Widening half-spread slightly and nudging skew up protects buy edge while keeping us competitive with the tightest rival (5.28). Pull protection left at 100bps/50 steps as drawdown neared trigger but did not fire.

Policy for next epoch: maintain size 3 and skew tilt, add small spread buffer against falling-market adverse selection.
